---
import GuideArticle from '../../../../components/GuideArticle.astro';
import { routeOf, GUIDE_BASE, routeDetailHref, hasRouteDetail } from '../../../../data/phone.js';

const voxi = routeOf('voxi-uk-esim-payg-retention')!;
const giff = routeOf('giffgaff-uk-direct-esim-payg')!;
const leb = routeOf('lebara-uk-direct-esim-china')!;
const three = routeOf('three-uk-payg-180d-2026')!;
const ee = routeOf('ee-uk-payg-180d-2026');
const o2Classic = routeOf('o2-uk-classic-payg-6mo-2026')!;
const vodafoneHold = routeOf('vodafone-uk-zero-esim-2026')!;

const guideRouteHref = (r: any) => routeDetailHref(r) || `${GUIDE_BASE}?route=${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}`;
const keepAliveHref = (r: any) => hasRouteDetail(r) ? `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/${r.id}/` : `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/#${r.id}`;
---
<GuideArticle slug="keep-uk-number-alive-abroad"
  h1="How to keep a UK phone number active while abroad"
  title="How to keep a UK phone number active while abroad (2026)"
  desc="Compare UK number keep-alive actions, first activation and overseas SMS uncertainty for VOXI, giffgaff, Lebara, Three, EE and legacy O2 Classic."
  lead="Keeping an already-activated UK number abroad is different from buying and activating one overseas. Provider rules, observed balance-changing actions, roaming reachability and app-specific verification outcomes can disagree; a cheap keep-alive action is not proof that first activation or incoming codes will work.">

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>The short answer</h2>
<p>For an <strong>existing, already usable</strong> line, <a href={guideRouteHref(voxi)}>VOXI</a> has a documented {voxi.keep?.intervalDays}-day balance-activity window and one dated small-charge example. <a href={guideRouteHref(giff)}>giffgaff</a> has a {giff.keep?.intervalDays}-day window but firsthand overseas accounts include both line survival and unexpected closure. <a href={guideRouteHref(leb)}>Lebara UK</a> has a {leb.keep?.intervalDays}-day keep window; a mainland-China incoming-SMS account conflicts with a separate no-signal/refund report, while provider instructions require UK service activation. None is a verified first-time-from-China checkout or named-bank OTP guarantee.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Three studied UK routes — different constraints</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>VOXI</strong> — {voxi.keep?.intervalDays}-day window; chargeable activity is required; a roaming SMS has been reported to count, but price/roaming and first activation remain location-specific. {voxi.keep?.action || ''}</li>
<li><strong>giffgaff</strong> — {giff.keep?.intervalDays}-day window; maintain evidenced activity but retain a recovery/port-out plan in view of conflicting closure reports. {giff.keep?.action || ''}</li>
<li><strong>Lebara UK</strong> — {leb.keep?.intervalDays}-day window for qualifying paid activity. Some community accounts recommend acting before the deadline; incoming codes, service activation and signal reception are different assertions. {leb.keep?.action || ''}</li>
</ul>
<p>Each route page carries the source evidence: <a href={guideRouteHref(voxi)}>VOXI</a> · <a href={guideRouteHref(giff)}>giffgaff</a> · <a href={guideRouteHref(leb)}>Lebara UK</a>.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>The MNO alternatives</h2>
<p><a href={guideRouteHref(three)}>Three UK</a>{ee && <> and <a href={guideRouteHref(ee)}>EE</a></>} both allow a {three.keep?.intervalDays}-day window with any chargeable activity. Three's standard PAYG rate is 10p/min, 10p/text; EE hibernates accounts after 180 days of no use.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>What changed in 2026 — O2 Classic PAYG is dead</h2>
<p>For years "O2 Classic PAYG at 2p per text every 6 months" was the standard advice. <strong>O2 has closed the tariff to new customers</strong> — the official O2 help page states you cannot switch to it unless you already hold it. If you see it recommended in an older guide, that guide is stale. We keep the <a href={guideRouteHref(o2Classic)}>O2 Classic PAYG entry</a> up as documentation, clearly marked not viable.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Vodafone UK — currently on hold</h2>
<p><a href={guideRouteHref(vodafoneHold)}>Vodafone UK PAYG</a>: no clean durable retention path is established. We show the hold reason instead of inventing a rule.</p></section>

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Never miss the window</h2>
<p>For a route you already control, use its <a href={keepAliveHref(voxi)}>deadline calculator</a> after verifying the last qualifying action and any grace/recovery rule. A missed window can lead to suspension or number loss; individual recovery options are not guaranteed.</p></section>
</GuideArticle>
